(a) Write the pseudo-code for a fully recursive function which copies a linked list?

FUNCTION printReverse(node)

    // Base case: if the current node is null,
    // there is nothing left to print
    IF node == null THEN
        RETURN
    END IF

    // Recursively move to the next node first
    // This continues until we reach the end of the list
    printReverse(node.next)

    // When the recursion unwinds (returns),
    // print the element stored at this node
    // This causes elements to be printed in reverse order
    PRINT node.element

END FUNCTION